le value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 163% of normal in June to July but only 65% in January to February. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 161% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 22672 had its driest year in 1953 at 65% of normal.</p>"}
